0,Kayan language (Borneo) - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kayan_language_(Borneo),"Kayan (Kajan, Kayan proper) is a dialect cluster spoken by the Kayan people of Borneo. It is a cluster of closely related dialects with limited mutual intelligibility, and is itself part of the Kayan-Murik group of Austronesian languages. Baram Kayan is a local trade language. [further explanation needed] Bahau is part of the dialect cluster, but is not ethnically Kayan.","Kayan, Baram",Austronesian
1,"Fieldwork on the music of the Kenyah and Kayan of Sarawak, Borneo ...",https://peklinkenyah.com/fieldwork,"The focus of my research was on Bornean songs for music education and choral performances. Initially, I visited the more easily accessible Kayan villages in the Lower Baram. Realising that Kenyah songs, with their wider melodious and harmonic variety, were more suitable for my purpose, I then ventured to the Upper Baram, focusing on the Kenyah.","Kayan, Baram",Austronesian
2,"Tekna': Lagu Tradisional Kayan | Tekna', Stories Through Songs",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HaxLIvGaOJ0,"Dokumentari ringkas mengenai Tekna' atau lagu/puisi tradisional masyarakat Kayan di Baram, Sarawak. Tekna' are usually performed at the end of a long day in the longhouse. As everyone relaxes ...","Kayan, Baram",Austronesian
3,KAYAN ETHNIC MUSIC - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rzuyb69hEgk,Traditional music of the Kayan people of Borneo,"Kayan, Baram",Austronesian
4,The Kenyah of Borneo : their culture and music — Kenyah songs research ...,https://peklinkenyah.com/kenyah-people,"Introduction: The Kenyah are an indigenous group dwelling in the mountainous plateau region and the upper reaches of four major rivers of Borneo (Baram and Balui rivers in Sarawak, and the Kayan and Mahakam rivers in Kalimantan). Despite living in relative isolation, mainly as subsistence farmers and migrating numerous times over the past two centuries, they have nurtured refined forms of the ...","Kayan, Baram",Austronesian
5,PDF THE KAYANS ORAL TRADITION OF BARAM - Universiti Malaysia Sarawak,https://ir.unimas.my/id/eprint/2679/1/DOCUMENTING.pdf,"Introduction the indigenous peoples of Sarawak. With my advantage as a Kayan, at least to begin with, my fellow researchers and I travelled to Miri, the northern city of Sarawak to conduct our field study on tekna‟, one of potentially extinct oral t dition among the Kayans of Baram. Equipped with two digita","Kayan, Baram",Austronesian
6,"Kayan, Baram Language (KYS) - Ethnologue (Free All)",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/kys/,"Baram Kayan is an endangered indigenous language of Malaysia. It belongs to the Austronesian language family. The language is used as a first language by all adults in the ethnic community, but not all young people. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Kayan, Baram",Austronesian
7,The Indigenous Music of Sarawak and Its Transmission Over ... - Springer,https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-981-16-4473-3_7,"The dance-songs, children's songs and basic dance movements of the Baram Kenyah and Kayan—Implications formusic education in Malaysia. [Unpublished masters's thesis].","Kayan, Baram",Austronesian
8,Songs from the Kenyah Community (2nd edition) - Areca Books,https://arecabooks.com/product/songs-from-the-kenyah-community-2nd-edition/,"The Kenyah are a minority indigenous ethnic group who dwell in the upper reaches of four rivers of Borneo (the Baram and Balui rivers of Sarawak, East Malaysia, and the Kayan and rivers in Kalimantan, Indonesia) and in the past, on two high plateaus (Usun Apau and Kayan), still referred to in their songs.","Kayan, Baram",Austronesian
9,Borneo Traditional - Melodigging,https://www.melodigging.com/genre/borneo-traditional,"Borneo traditional is an umbrella term for the ritual, ceremonial, and community music of the island of Borneo—especially among Dayak and Orang Ulu peoples (Kenyah, Kayan, Penan, Iban), as well as Bidayuh, Kadazan-Dusun, Melanau, and Bruneian Malay communities.","Kayan, Baram",Austronesian
